---
import MainLayout from '@/layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import LegalFooter from '@/components/LegalFooter.astro';
import {
  LEGAL_OPERATOR_LOCATION,
  LEGAL_OPERATOR_NAME,
  TRADING_NAME,
} from '@/lib/legal/businessIdentity';
import { SAAS_EXPORT_RETENTION_DAYS } from '@/lib/setup/saasEntitlement';
import { PAGE_DESCRIPTIONS } from '@/lib/seo/defaults';
import '@/styles/legal-pages.css';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Kersivo"
  description={PAGE_DESCRIPTIONS.privacy}
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="container legal-page__inner">
      <h1 class="legal-page__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated: 25 September 2026</p>

      <p>
        This policy describes how personal data is processed when you use websites and services operated under the
        KERSIVO brand for UK barbershops, including marketing pages, live product preview booking and shop flows,
        monthly subscription checkout, and (where applicable) the barbershop admin experience. It is written in plain
        language and does not replace legal advice.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Note:</strong> The live public offer is a <strong>£39/month</strong> {TRADING_NAME} SaaS subscription
        paid via Stripe Checkout on {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s own Stripe account. There is no current public setup-fee
        offer. Legacy setup-deposit checkout creation is disabled; any historical setup-deposit records may still be
        supported for fulfilment and customer support.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible for your data?</h2>
      <p>
        The legal operator of the {TRADING_NAME} service is <strong>{LEGAL_OPERATOR_NAME}</strong>, trading as
        {TRADING_NAME}, based in {LEGAL_OPERATOR_LOCATION}. References in this policy to &ldquo;{TRADING_NAME}&rdquo;,
        &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo; and &ldquo;our&rdquo; mean {LEGAL_OPERATOR_NAME} trading as {TRADING_NAME},
        unless the context refers specifically to a barbershop using the service.
      </p>
      <p>
        {TRADING_NAME} is <strong>not</strong> the controller for every category of personal data processed through the
        platform. Roles depend on whose relationship with the data subject is involved.
      </p>

      <h3>When the barbershop is the controller</h3>
      <p>
        Where a live barbershop uses {TRADING_NAME} to run its own booking, client records, notes, retail pickup, staff
        roster or related operational tools, that <strong>barbershop determines the purposes and means</strong> of
        processing personal data about its customers, clients, barbers and team members. In those cases, the barbershop
        is the <strong>data controller</strong>, and {TRADING_NAME} processes that personal data
        <strong>on the barbershop&rsquo;s behalf</strong> as a <strong>processor</strong> to provide the software
        service (for example hosting bookings, sending transactional confirmations or reminders, and storing client CRM
        records).
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are a customer of a barbershop that uses {TRADING_NAME}, you should normally contact that barbershop first
        about your personal data. {TRADING_NAME} can assist the barbershop where appropriate. The contractual terms for
        {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s processor role with business Clients are set out in the
        <a href="/dpa">Data Processing Agreement</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>When {TRADING_NAME} is an independent controller</h3>
      <p>
        {TRADING_NAME} remains an <strong>independent controller</strong> for personal data it processes for its own
        business purposes, including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>{TRADING_NAME} account-holder details and authentication / security records;</li>
        <li>subscription and billing administration;</li>
        <li>terms acceptance and related contract records;</li>
        <li>support and contact enquiries sent directly to {TRADING_NAME};</li>
        <li>direct communications between {TRADING_NAME} and the business customer (the barbershop);</li>
        <li>B2B prospecting and business outreach to relevant UK barbershop contacts;</li>
        <li>tax, accounting and legal records {TRADING_NAME} must keep;</li>
        <li>consented analytics on {TRADING_NAME} marketing pages;</li>
        <li>fraud, security and abuse-prevention records; and</li>
        <li>{TRADING_NAME} operational audit records.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For data protection enquiries about {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s own controller processing, or to exercise rights
        relating to that data, contact:
        <a href="mailto:hello@kersivo.co.uk">hello@kersivo.co.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What data we process and why</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may process:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact and setup enquiries</strong> — name, email address and message content you submit through our
          contact form. <strong>Purpose:</strong> responding to your request. <strong>Legal basis (UK):</strong>
          legitimate interests. ({TRADING_NAME} as independent controller.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>SaaS subscription billing (£39/month)</strong> — when you subscribe via Stripe Checkout on
          {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s platform Stripe account, we process business-customer billing details such as name,
          email, shop/business details needed for fulfilment, payment status, amount/currency, and Stripe-generated
          customer, subscription, Checkout session and related payment identifiers. Stripe hosts card entry;
          {TRADING_NAME} does <strong>not</strong> receive or store full card numbers or CVC.
          <strong>Purpose:</strong> taking and administering the subscription, confirming payment, onboarding and
          related fulfilment notices. <strong>Legal basis (UK):</strong> performance of a contract / steps prior to a
          contract where you are personally the contracting party; legitimate interests where we process contact or
          administrative details of representatives of a corporate customer for billing and fulfilment administration.
          Specific accounting or tax records may also be processed where a UK legal obligation requires them.
          ({TRADING_NAME} as independent controller for this billing relationship.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>B2B prospecting and business outreach</strong> — {TRADING_NAME} may identify relevant UK barbershop
          business prospects from public business sources. Personal data may include a business contact name or role,
          public business contact information, public social handles, and business-related research or outreach history.
          Sources may include business websites, public social profiles, Companies House where relevant, and other
          public business sources. <strong>Purpose:</strong> relevant B2B prospecting, direct outreach and
          administration (including follow-ups, replies and do-not-contact / suppression records).
          <strong>Legal basis (UK):</strong> legitimate interests where applicable, and only where separate PECR rules
          for electronic marketing are satisfied. Legitimate interests is <strong>not</strong> treated as permission to
          message individual subscribers (for example many sole traders) where PECR requires consent.
          Tools used for this work include Notion for lead administration, Google/Gmail for email, and Meta/Instagram
          where direct messaging is used — without claiming unverified processor contracts or transfer conclusions for
          those tools. Retention follows prospect and suppression rules (personal contact research not yet contacted is
          either notified within 30 days or personal contact fields are removed; unsuccessful personal outreach history
          is generally removed or anonymised after about six months; minimal suppression data may be kept longer solely
          to honour an objection). You have an <strong>absolute right to object</strong> to use of your personal data
          for direct marketing. Object by replying to the message or emailing
          <a href="mailto:hello@kersivo.co.uk">hello@kersivo.co.uk</a>. ({TRADING_NAME} as independent controller.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Historical setup deposits (not currently offered)</strong> — where a legacy setup-deposit Checkout
          session was created historically, name, email, shop details and payment status may still be held for
          fulfilment and support. New setup-deposit Checkout creation is disabled. ({TRADING_NAME} as independent
          controller for those historical billing records.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Campaign / source information</strong> — campaign or source parameters (for example gclid, gbraid,
          wbraid or UTM values) may appear in the page URL. Where you grant Analytics consent, consent-based website
          analytics (GA4) may process relevant campaign/source information as part of ordinary analytics measurement
          (see Website analytics below). {TRADING_NAME} does <strong>not</strong> separately persist those checkout
          campaign identifiers into Stripe Checkout metadata or internal fulfilment email. There is no dedicated
          {TRADING_NAME} attribution cookie or localStorage. Google Ads website tags remain inactive on Production.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Optional Sign in with Google</strong> — where offered (for example &ldquo;Continue with Google&rdquo;),
          you may sign in or create a {TRADING_NAME} business/admin account using your Google Account. Google provides
          identity information needed for that login, which may include a Google account identifier, email address,
          email verification status, name, and profile picture URL. <strong>Purpose:</strong> authenticating you,
          creating and maintaining your {TRADING_NAME} business/admin account, account linking where applicable, and
          onboarding / account display. This is <strong>not</strong> used for end-customer booking login.
          <strong>Legal basis (UK):</strong> performance of a contract where you are personally the contracting party
          and Google Sign-In is necessary to provide the account access you requested; legitimate interests where you are
          staff, a manager or a representative of a corporate customer using Google Sign-In for authorised business
          access. {TRADING_NAME} does <strong>not</strong> request access to Gmail, Google Drive, Calendar, Contacts or other
          Google account content through this login. Under the current implementation, {TRADING_NAME} does
          <strong>not</strong> durably retain Google OAuth access tokens, refresh tokens or ID tokens after
          authentication. Google separately processes your Google Account information under
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
            >Google&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a
          >. ({TRADING_NAME} as independent controller for this account/authentication data.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Booking data (live barbershop)</strong> — service, barber, date/time, and contact details (name and
          email; phone if provided). Processed so the barbershop can manage appointments, confirmations, reschedule and
          cancel links, and related emails. On a live tenant site the <strong>barbershop is the controller</strong>;
          {TRADING_NAME} processes this data as <strong>processor</strong>. Demo / sandbox booking flows on the
          marketing site are simulations or previews and are described separately where they apply.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Shop orders (buy-and-collect)</strong> — for a <strong>live</strong> barbershop shop: email address
          used at checkout, order contents, payment status as recorded after payment, and related confirmation emails to
          fulfil your purchase. Card payments are handled securely by <strong>Stripe</strong> on the
          <strong>barbershop&rsquo;s connected Stripe account</strong> (Stripe Connect Express / direct charges). The
          barbershop remains the seller and controller for that customer payment; {TRADING_NAME} facilitates the
          technical checkout flow and does <strong>not</strong> charge an application/platform commission (Stripe&rsquo;s
          own processing fees are separate). {TRADING_NAME} does not store full card numbers or CVC. The barbershop is
          typically the controller of retail customer data; {TRADING_NAME} processes related shop records as processor
          to run the shop software. The public retail demo on this marketing site is a simulation only and does not
          collect checkout personal data, take payment, or create an order. Private owner test orders in admin may
          create marked test records without payment.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Booking deposits (live barbershop)</strong> — where enabled, booking deposits are taken through the
          barbershop&rsquo;s connected Stripe account under the same Connect model (barbershop seller/controller;
          {TRADING_NAME} facilitator; no {TRADING_NAME} application fee). {TRADING_NAME} may store limited payment
          status and Stripe identifiers needed to operate the booking software, not full card details.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Post-purchase setup</strong> — after a KERSIVO subscription purchase, information you submit in the
          authenticated KERSIVO client onboarding (for example business details, branding, team, services, opening hours,
          photos and migration notes) is processed to prepare your barbershop for launch.
          ({TRADING_NAME} as independent controller for the business-customer relationship; some fields may also relate
          to staff or migration content controlled by the barbershop once live.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Admin access</strong> — first-party session cookies / tokens that keep you signed in to the
          barbershop admin panel (typically for up to 30 days), and operational logs needed for security.
          ({TRADING_NAME} as independent controller for account security.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Content you upload</strong> — for example barber or product images where the product allows uploads.
          Stored so the site and shop can display them. Client-note images on a live shop are processed for the
          barbershop as controller.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email delivery</strong> — we use <strong>Resend</strong> to send transactional emails (for example
          booking confirmations, order confirmations, subscription fulfilment notices, and contact form delivery to our
          inbox), using the addresses involved in each message. Booking and retail customer emails for a live shop are
          sent as processor on the barbershop&rsquo;s behalf; {TRADING_NAME} account and marketing emails are
          {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s own controller processing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Website analytics (optional)</strong> — if you accept Analytics cookies on {TRADING_NAME} marketing
          pages, Google Analytics 4 may process pseudonymous usage data (for example pages viewed and approximate
          location derived by Google) to help us understand site performance. Live barbershop booking and storefront
          pages do not load {TRADING_NAME} marketing analytics tags.
          <strong>Legal basis (UK):</strong> consent. For the current configuration (Google &ldquo;Google products &amp;
          services&rdquo; data sharing off), Google acts as a <strong>processor</strong> for Analytics-service data
          processed to provide the Analytics service; {TRADING_NAME} remains the controller for deciding to use GA4 on
          the marketing site. The standard Google Analytics contractual provider is <strong>Google Ireland Limited</strong>.
          Transfers to Ireland are covered by UK adequacy regulations. Google may process data internationally and use
          subprocessors; for applicable onward transfers to the United States, Google documents use of the UK Extension
          to the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework where coverage applies, and otherwise relies on the transfer mechanisms
          in its data processing terms (including applicable Standard Contractual Clauses).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Ads (currently inactive)</strong> — Production does not currently configure Google Ads
          measurement IDs, conversion labels, or remarketing tags. Cookie settings do not currently offer Advertising
          measurement or Personalised advertising choices. We do <strong>not</strong> use Google Ads Enhanced
          Conversions. This does not claim that any historical Google-held Ads records were erased from Google&rsquo;s
          systems.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>SMS (optional)</strong> — if you subscribe to a plan that includes SMS and we enable it for your shop,
          we may process mobile numbers and message content needed to send appointment reminders through a third-party
          SMS provider, only where that feature is enabled. For live-shop reminders the barbershop is the controller and
          {TRADING_NAME} acts as processor.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Recipients and providers</h2>
      <p>
        To provide the live barbershop service, {TRADING_NAME} uses infrastructure providers that may process Customer
        Personal Data as <strong>sub-processors</strong> (on {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s behalf as processor for the
        barbershop), including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — application hosting;</li>
        <li><strong>Neon</strong> / <strong>PostgreSQL</strong> — database hosting;</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> — transactional email delivery;</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Twilio</strong> — SMS delivery, only where SMS reminders are enabled for a shop;
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sentry</strong> — application error monitoring, only where monitoring is configured;
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>OpenAI</strong> — language-model processing for the optional admin AI assistant, only where the
          assistant is enabled. Free-text prompts submitted by authorised Client users may contain Customer Personal
          Data and are processed to generate responses. {TRADING_NAME} does not automatically export Client tenant
          databases to OpenAI.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Other providers are used in specific functional contexts and are not listed above as general sub-processors:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Stripe</strong> — payment services for (a) {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s own £39/month SaaS subscription
          billing on {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s platform Stripe account, and (b) live barbershop booking deposits and retail
          payments through the barbershop&rsquo;s connected Stripe account (Stripe Connect Express; merchants collect
          payments directly; {TRADING_NAME} application fee is 0%). Stripe processes card payments; {TRADING_NAME} does
          not store full card numbers or CVC. Under Stripe&rsquo;s terms, Stripe may process personal data both as a
          processor for User-directed payment services and as an independent controller for fraud prevention,
          regulatory, compliance and other Stripe purposes. Stripe is therefore <strong>not</strong> listed above as a
          general {TRADING_NAME} Customer Personal Data sub-processor merely because Connect payments are facilitated.
          The public retail demo does not use Stripe Checkout.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Sign-In</strong> — optional identity / authentication for {TRADING_NAME} business/admin
          accounts (see &ldquo;Optional Sign in with Google&rdquo; above). This is separate from Google Analytics /
          Ads.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> — optional Analytics measurement on {TRADING_NAME} marketing pages only
          when you consent (see the Cookie Policy). ACTIVE / consent-based. These tags are not used on live barbershop
          booking or storefront pages. Separate from Google Sign-In. Google products &amp; services data sharing is off
          for the current Analytics account configuration. Direct contractual provider: Google Ireland Limited
          (adequacy-covered UK→Ireland path; Google may process internationally under its processing terms as described
          under &ldquo;Website analytics&rdquo; above).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Ads</strong> — INACTIVE / DORMANT on Production (no Ads measurement ID / purchase conversion
          label configured; no active Ads consent choice in Cookie settings). Historical use may exist in older Google
          account records; those are not claimed erased here. Separate from Google Sign-In and from GA4.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal data. Where we engage providers to process Customer Personal Data on a barbershop&rsquo;s
        behalf, we do so under appropriate arrangements required by UK data protection law.
      </p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Data may be processed by providers outside the UK (for example in the United States). Where that happens, we
        rely on approved safeguard mechanisms required by UK data protection law (for example the UK International Data
        Transfer Agreement / Addendum or Standard Contractual Clauses), as offered by those providers. Details of each
        provider&rsquo;s transfer mechanism should be confirmed in their current data processing terms.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
      <p>
        Retention depends on whose data it is and why it is held. Personal data should not be kept longer than needed
        for its purpose. Different categories can have different, purpose-specific periods.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Live barbershop (Customer Personal Data).</strong> While a subscription is active, shop customer and
          booking data is kept to run the service under the barbershop&rsquo;s instructions.
          {TRADING_NAME} does <strong>not</strong> independently apply a blanket deletion period to active shop
          customer/booking records. After a subscription ends, the barbershop may export a free CSV of client contact
          details and booking history for up to <strong>{SAAS_EXPORT_RETENTION_DAYS} days</strong>. After that window,
          the live shop data graph is eligible to be permanently deleted from the production database. Cancellation does
          <strong>not</strong> delete shop data instantly. An explicit account deletion (or another documented lawful
          instruction from the barbershop) may end live shop retention earlier than that default window. Where the
          barbershop is the controller, authorised barbershop admins can also instruct {TRADING_NAME} to erase an
          individual customer&rsquo;s profile and related customer-controlled data (for example notes). Historical
          booking or payment records may remain in anonymised or minimised form where retention is still needed for
          operational, payment, accounting, legal or dispute purposes. Active or unresolved appointments, payments or
          in-flight messages may temporarily prevent erasure until resolved. Residual copies may remain temporarily in
          encrypted backups or other provider systems until those copies expire or are deleted
          under the provider&rsquo;s normal lifecycle; we do not promise immediate physical erasure from every
          backup or provider replica.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>{TRADING_NAME} independent-controller records.</strong> Account, billing, tax, legal acceptance,
          security and operational audit records may be retained for separate, purpose-specific periods needed for those
          purposes (for example limited billing and legal-acceptance evidence may be kept for up to six years after the
          end of the relevant commercial relationship, unless a live dispute or legal obligation requires longer). That
          does <strong>not</strong> mean all personal data of every type is kept for six years, and it is
          <strong>not</strong> a claim that UK GDPR itself imposes a single six-year retention rule for everything.
          Cancelling a subscription does <strong>not</strong> necessarily delete Stripe-held financial/payment records
          immediately; Stripe&rsquo;s own retention of payment data is controlled by Stripe. {TRADING_NAME}
          account-deletion workflows also do not currently delete every provider-side Stripe Customer or Subscription
          record. Local deletion likewise does not guarantee immediate erasure of every residual copy held by other
          providers (for example email, SMS, monitoring, hosting or AI providers where used).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics and advertising cookies</strong> follow the durations in our
          <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a> when you have consented.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights (UK)</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018, you may have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>request access to your personal data;</li>
        <li>ask for inaccurate data to be corrected;</li>
        <li>ask for data to be erased in certain circumstances (this right is not absolute and may be limited where
          retention is still needed for a legal obligation or to establish, exercise or defend legal claims);</li>
        <li>restrict or object to processing in certain circumstances;</li>
        <li>object to processing of your personal data for direct marketing (this right is absolute);</li>
        <li>data portability where applicable;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If your request relates to a barbershop&rsquo;s customers or bookings, contact that barbershop first (they are
        usually the controller). {TRADING_NAME} provides tools and assistance so the barbershop can action valid erasure
        instructions for customer profile and related data, subject to lawful retention and technical limits described
        above. For {TRADING_NAME} account, billing or marketing data, email
        <a href="mailto:hello@kersivo.co.uk">hello@kersivo.co.uk</a>. You may also complain to the UK Information
        Commissioner&rsquo;s Office (ICO):
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/">https://ico.org.uk/</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>
        We use necessary cookies and similar technologies to run the website (for example security, payments-related
        flows, forms, remembering your privacy choices, and keeping a barbershop admin signed in). With your permission
        on {TRADING_NAME} marketing pages, we also use analytics technologies as described in our
        <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Admin login uses necessary first-party session cookies so you can stay signed in while managing your shop. Full
        names, purposes and durations are listed in the Cookie Policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can accept, reject or change optional technologies at any time using
        <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the website footer, or by revisiting the cookie banner when your consent
        version is updated.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We apply appropriate technical and organisational measures appropriate to the nature of the service, including
        access controls for admin areas and encrypted connections (HTTPS) for site traffic. No online service can be
        guaranteed 100% secure.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date will change when we do. We will
        notify active clients of any material changes via email. Material changes to cookie purposes may also require a
        new consent choice.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <LegalFooter />
</MainLayout>
